P01-S1 is done and committed (`1364f0f`): the pen ink works on the tablet (the fast on-screen layer is present), each pen event takes 0.28 ms of UI-thread time at p95 against a 1 ms budget, and all 9 screenshots taken after lifting the pen show the complete stroke. ADR-002 is now Accepted.
The ink hand-off now waits until the frame that draws the finished stroke is on its way to the screen. The frame timer the spec called for fires one step too early, so amendment A-005 changes the spec. The app asks for 144 Hz but the tablet stays at 120 Hz, probably capped by the HyperOS refresh-rate setting. Screenshots can't catch a one-frame flicker, so two checks are added under USER-CHECK: how the pen feels compared with Xiaomi Notes, and that refresh setting.
Next is P01-S2, the renderer spike. The spike code and its `spike-ink` screen stay until P01-T08 removes or promotes them.
